# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Exclude most of the Maven target directory to keep the build context small.
# We use a negation rule to allow only the final repackaged JAR through —
# that is the only file Dockerfile.backend needs to COPY into the image.
# Without this exception, Docker would fail with "file not found" during COPY.
target/
!target/auctionSystem-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar

# ── Local SQLite database files ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: Never bake local DB files into the image. The containers use a
# Docker named volume (bidtech-data) mounted at /app/data/ instead.
# If these were included, local test data could leak into the production image.
*.db

# ── Git metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No need to ship version control history inside the image.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── Maven wrapper internals ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Maven wrapper is only needed to build the JAR (done in deploy.ps1 on the host).
# It is not needed inside the container at runtime.
.mvn/

# ── Documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Markdown files are for humans, not containers.
*.md

# ── IDE and Eclipse project files ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are local developer configuration files with no runtime value.
.settings/
.classpath
.project
.vscode/

# ── Postman collections ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API test collections are developer tooling, not application code.
postman/
